No.  It really actually _isn't_ better.  It teaches people to be scared
of something that they don't need to be scared of.  Half of the skill
involving in beating this game like a drum is to learn to quit listening 
to the urban legends propounded by old-timers about "how hard it is", 
and move into the 21st century, where very efficient strategies have 
been developed.  

(Interestingly, the urban legends were _somewhat_ true back in 1994; the
spoiler tree hadn't been so fully developed, and there wasn't anything
like NAO around to allow people to conveniently watch each others' games
and learn not from their own mistakes, but from others'.  But we are in
2009 now, not 1994 -- 15 years later.  The world has changed, the world
around Nethack has changed.  It is time to upgrade our perceptions to
the modern reality, which is:  Nethack is solved.

Oh, hey, did you know Mikko Juola (Adeon) now has a 29-game ascension
streak on NAO?  That passes both Mike Kelly and Christian Bressler
(marvin).  Think that's accidental, or do you think perhaps there's some
truth to the matter that Nethack just isn't that hard a game, if you 
actually try to win?)

